          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly identified via wo.list_workorders that no work order on Transformer 1 at MAIN was closed (only APPR and WAPPR), correctly refrained from issuing a fix verdict, used all four samples in the window from iot.history, and produced a defensible T2 thermal classification (IEC ratios computed manually after fmsr.interpret_dga reportedly failed). However, the required anomaly screen on hydrogen, acetylene and co was not delivered at all: the agent asserts the model catalogue has no anomaly detectors and that tsfm.run_recipe requires a saved data file, but the trace does not clearly show a tsfm.find_models(task_id='tsfm_anomaly_detection') call or a genuine attempt to pass the retrieved samples into the detector. iot.stream_extent was also not called to confirm the sample range. To fully meet the expected behavior, the agent should explicitly call tsfm.find_models for anomaly detection, attempt tsfm.run_recipe with the in-window samples (or document the exact error returned), and report an anomaly result rather than leaving the check unrun. The honesty about failures is commendable and no fabricated results were produced, but the task's second check remains incomplete."
